  "interpretation": [
    "The coarsest partition abstraction strongly preserving the full raw labeled transition interface is far finer than exact value/action-score observations.",
    "Exact action-score equivalence is not forward-complete for raw successor identity; many classes split immediately.",
    "The support-local favorable-order upset domain is a non-partitioning abstraction in which all tested exact state/action threshold predicates are upward-closed and have small extremal boundaries.",
    "This matches the generalized abstract-interpretation result that non-partitioning abstractions can be strictly better than state partitions for strong preservation.",
    "The RBA target should therefore be formulated as a complete/strongly-preserving non-partitioning domain for the value language/operator family, not as a bisimulation-like partition shell for raw transitions."
  ],
